Third-party work
----------------

Arithmetic-coded JPEG (pas/pjajpeg.pas, the QM coder section): the decoder
and encoder follow libjpeg's jdarith.c and jcarith.c, and the Qe table is
taken from libjpeg-turbo's jaricom.c. This software is based in part on the
work of the Independent JPEG Group.

JPEG-LS (pas/pjajls.pas): written from ITU-T T.87, with its behaviour
where the standard leaves room (the bit stuffing, the padding at the end of
a scan, the bounds on the context variables, the Golomb code limits)
following CharLS 2.4.2, whose decoding and encoding it reproduces bit for
bit. CharLS is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause license:

